---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '31 July 2026';

// Functional browser-storage keys. Keep in sync with the code that sets them:
// theme.ts, i18n.ts, CardTable.tsx, and the inline preference script in BaseLayout.astro.
const storageKeys = [
  { key: 'otogidb-theme', purpose: 'Light or dark mode' },
  { key: 'otogidb-style-variant', purpose: 'Classic or Spirit Scroll styling' },
  { key: 'otogidb-locale', purpose: 'Your chosen language' },
  { key: 'otogidb-show-bugs', purpose: 'Whether known-bug notices are shown' },
  { key: 'otogidb-lb-mode', purpose: 'Whether card stats are shown at LB0 or MLB' },
  {
    key: 'otogidb-maintenance-dismissed',
    purpose: 'Which site notice you dismissed, so it stays hidden',
  },
];

const processors = [
  {
    name: 'Cloudflare',
    purpose: 'Hosts the site and delivers it worldwide',
    href: 'https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/',
  },
  {
    name: 'Cloudinary',
    purpose: 'Delivers card images',
    href: 'https://cloudinary.com/privacy',
  },
  {
    name: 'PostHog',
    purpose: 'Page-view counts and error reports (United States)',
    href: 'https://posthog.com/privacy',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How OtogiDB handles your data: no accounts, no ads, no tracking cookies."
>
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 py-8 max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm mb-8" style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
      Last updated: {lastUpdated}
    </p>

    <div
      class="rounded-lg border p-4 mb-8"
      style="border-color: var(--color-border); background-color: var(--color-surface);"
    >
      <h2 class="font-bold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">The short version</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        OtogiDB has no accounts, no ads, and no tracking cookies. We don't know who you are
        and we don't try to find out. We count page views so we can tell which pages are
        useful and whether something is broken. That's it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">Who runs this site</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        OtogiDB is a small, independently run fan project. For anything relating to privacy,
        contact <a href="mailto:privacy@otogidb.com" class="link">privacy@otogidb.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">What we don't do</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1" style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        <li>No user accounts, sign-ups, or logins</li>
        <li>No advertising and no advertising networks</li>
        <li>No tracking cookies</li>
        <li>No session recording, heatmaps, or scroll tracking</li>
        <li>No profiles built about you, and no attempt to recognise you across visits</li>
        <li>We never sell or share your data</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">
        What's stored on your device
      </h2>
      <p class="mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        We store a few settings in your browser so the site remembers how you like it. These
        are preferences you choose. They stay in your browser, are never sent to us, and
        clearing your site data removes them.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        {storageKeys.map(({ key, purpose }) => (
          <li><code class="text-sm">{key}</code> &mdash; {purpose}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        The site also installs a service worker, which caches pages and images so it loads
        faster and keeps working on a poor connection. It stores site content, not
        information about you.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3" style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        Nothing is stored on your device for analytics.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">Analytics</h2>
      <p class="mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        We use PostHog to count page views. It is configured to store nothing at all on your
        device &mdash; no cookie, no browser storage. For each page view we record the page
        address, the referring page, your browser and device type, and an approximate country.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        Because nothing is stored on your device, we cannot tell whether you are a new or
        returning visitor, and we cannot follow you from one page to the next. Our visitor
        numbers are rough counts, which is all we need them to be.
      </p>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        If your browser sends a "Do Not Track" signal, we don't record anything at all.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">Error reporting</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        When something breaks, the error is reported to PostHog so we find out about it. These
        reports describe what went wrong in the code and which page it happened on. They don't
        contain anything you typed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">
        Who processes data for us
      </h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr style="color: var(--color-text);">
              <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Provider</th>
              <th class="py-2 font-semibold">What they do</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
            {processors.map(({ name, purpose, href }) => (
              <tr class="border-t" style="border-color: var(--color-border);">
                <td class="py-2 pr-4 whitespace-nowrap">
                  <a href={href} class="link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{name}</a>
                </td>
                <td class="py-2">{purpose}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">IP addresses</h2>
      <p class="mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        Every website receives your IP address &mdash; it is how the page reaches you. Our
        analytics is configured to discard it: your IP is used briefly to work out an
        approximate country and to filter out bot traffic, then thrown away. It is never
        stored alongside anything you did on the site.
      </p>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        Cloudflare and Cloudinary necessarily handle your IP address in order to send you the
        site and its images, under their own privacy policies linked above.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">
        How long we keep things
      </h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        Page-view and error records are kept for one year and then deleted. Because they
        contain no identifier for you, they cannot be connected back to you at any point.
        Settings saved in your browser stay until you clear your site data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">Your rights</h2>
      <p class="mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        If you are in the UK, EU, or another region with similar laws, you have the right to
        access your personal data, have it corrected or deleted, object to how it is used, and
        complain to your data protection authority.
      </p>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        In practice there is usually nothing for us to act on. We store no identifier for you,
        so we have no way to find records relating to any particular person &mdash; there is
        nothing to look up, hand over, or delete. If you think we hold something about you,
        write to <a href="mailto:privacy@otogidb.com" class="link">privacy@otogidb.com</a> and
        we'll look into it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">Children</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        This site is not aimed at children, and we don't knowingly collect information about
        anyone. Since we collect no personal information from any visitor, no special handling
        applies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">Links to other sites</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        We link to places like GitHub and the app stores. Following one of those links takes
        you somewhere with its own privacy policy, which we don't control. Simply having the
        link on the page sends nothing to them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">
        Changes to this policy
      </h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        If we change how any of this works, we'll update this page and the date at the top.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section
      class="rounded-lg border p-4"
      style="border-color: var(--color-border); background-color: var(--color-surface);"
    >
      <h2 class="font-bold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">Not an official site</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
        OtogiDB is an unofficial fan project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
        connected to the publisher or developers of Otogi: Spirit Agents. Game names, images,
        and data remain the property of their respective owners.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
